    "result": "{\"analysis\":\"Avg bits 3.147953869047619 leaves almost no room under the 403/128 budget, so these four proposals change options only and keep every cell unchanged. The upgrade options don't pay off. Moving one 3.1M-param MLP layer up a bit costs about the same as dropping another one from int3 to int2. Every measured int3→int2 drop on an MLP layer adds more than 0.018 KL, which outweighs any single upgrade's gain. Each concentration layer already uses the best 3-bit method its row measured. Last round's proposals were refused only because they quoted a rounded whole-recipe KL. These versions resubmit them without that number.\",\"stop\":false,\"proposals\":[{\"name\":\"opt_act_order_v2\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true}},\"rationale\":\"Costs no bits. The loss sits in GPTQ-quantized MLP layers, for example rht_gptq_int2 on layer 14 down_proj at 0.00633466 [E4c3f9b73e065] and gptq_int3 on layer 27 up_proj at 0.0057182 [Ef04d8aa7bded]. Layer 27 up_proj has activation kurtosis 1090.09 [E24beed188b6a]. Setting weight_algo.act_order=true quantizes the high-activation columns first. The whole-recipe KL is in [E514ab09c524e].\",\"cites\":[\"E4c3f9b73e065\",\"Ef04d8aa7bded\",\"E24beed188b6a\",\"E514ab09c524e\"]},{\"name\":\"opt_damp_low_v2\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005}},\"rationale\":\"Costs no bits. Lowering to weight_algo.damp=0.005 makes the GPTQ error compensation follow the Hessian more closely. That should help the MLP layers that carry the loss, such as layer 3 up_proj with rht_gptq_int3 at 0.0064177 [E6f4f7ea296d5]. The baseline is in [E514ab09c524e].\",\"cites\":[\"E6f4f7ea296d5\",\"E514ab09c524e\"]},{\"name\":\"opt_damp_high_v2\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05}},\"rationale\":\"Costs no bits. Raising to weight_algo.damp=0.05 stabilizes GPTQ on layers with heavy-tailed activations. Layer 27 gate_proj has activation kurtosis 1090.09 [E5aee24c5494a] and its rht_gptq_int3 KL is 0.00498703 [Efa0bb391da67]. The baseline is in [E514ab09c524e].\",\"cites\":[\"E5aee24c5494a\",\"Efa0bb391da67\",\"E514ab09c524e\"]},{\"name\":\"opt_act_order_damp_low\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true,\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true,\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true,\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true,\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true,\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true,\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005}},\"rationale\":\"Costs no bits. Combines weight_algo.act_order=true with weight_algo.damp=0.005 for the GPTQ layers that carry the loss, for example layer 18 gate_proj with rht_gptq_int2 at kl_minus_floor 0.00497017293625499 [Eb1dd74cd6447]. The baseline is in [E514ab09c524e].\",\"cites\":[\"Eb1dd74cd6447\",\"E514ab09c524e\"]}]}",
